%S: (original ABC: "learned from the Lúnasa album")
%D: 2001: Lúnasa: Merry Sisters of Fate
%D: 2005: An Spiorad: Cúig
%D: 2007: Kieran Fahy: Trip to Ireland (Compilation)
%D: 2012: Lúnasa with the RTÉ Concert Orchestra
%D: 2018: Dannsair: Celtic Meditations
N: Comment from ManekiNenu on thesession.org:
N: Coyí d?un artu una flor
N: That?s the actual name of this Asturian traditional "tonada" arranged for flute by Marcos Llope, flute player from the Asturian folk band Llan de Cubel. It was included at the album "IV". Asturian tonadas are a kind of traditional liric vocal songs without time. Sometimes they are accompanied by the Asturian bagpipes.
N: Coyí d?un artu una flor = I took a flower from a [bramble], in Asturian language
M: 4/4
L: 1/8
Q: 1/4=70
