%%text TS11 - French and English

X:103
T:Calvin Cycle, The 
C:Ethan Hazzard-Watkins,  2008 
N:The light-independent (a.k.a. "dark") reactions of the Calvin Cycle comprise the second half of Photosynthesis, 
N:during which plants use energy captured from sunlight to convert carbon dioxide into glucose. 
N:I wrote this tune in 2008 and have played it often with Elixir as well as teaching it in several workshops. 
N:It languished without a title until 2014 when Kathleen and Jim Fownes (of the band Light Reaction) started 
N:sharing it. The title is a nod to their band name in appreciation of their enthusiasm for the tune. 
