C:as played by various bands including Blowzabella
M:4/4
N:We know this tune as Nobel Franz, but it was originally called "Mominette", by the composer.
%N: To make matters even more confusing it has also been passed around as "Schottische a Bethanie"
N:It's also been jiggified by U Hornby as "The Plane Tree".
% Mominette is the second tune in each of these videos, after Derriere les Carreaux
% at 2:44 :
F:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GQrt4Q6lk9Q
% the Bruno Bizis Band, proving there's no such thing as too many accordions,
% at 2:59 :
F:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oc0dhrG-F-4
% The second video shows couples dancing, not the schottische we know at Mt. Airy Contra as of 2020.
Z:Adlai Waksman
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:Em
