%%column 2
%%text CHORUS:
%%text He goes wa wa wa waltzing, waltzing with bears
%%text Raggy bears, shaggy bears, baggy bears too
%%text There's nothing on earth Uncle Walter won't do
%%text So he can go waltzing, wa wa wa waltzing
%%text He can go waltzing, waltzing with bears
%%text
%%text VERSE:
%%text I went to his room in the middle of the night, I tiptoed in and I turned on the light
%%text But to my surprise, he was nowhere in sight, For my Uncle Walter goes waltzing at night
%%text (CHORUS)
%%text 
%%text We gave Uncle Walter a new coat to wear, When he came home it was covered with hair
%%text Lately I've noticed several new tears, I think Uncle Walter's been waltzing with bears
%%text (CHORUS)
%%text 
%%text We told Uncle Walter that he should be good, Do all the things that we think he should
%%text But I know that he'd rather be out in the wood, I'm afraid we might lose Uncle Walter for good
%%text (CHORUS)
%%text 
%%text Well we begged and we pleaded, "Oh please won't you stay", Managed to keep him at home for a day
%%text But the bears all barged in and they took him away, Now he's dancing with pandas, 
%%text And he can't understand us, And the bears all demand at least one waltz a day
%%text (CHORUS)
